 "final_text": "**Answer for Sam:**\n\nYes, Meadow Analytics **was** invoiced \u2014 that's why you can't find them: the invoice never made it into the ERP or Books.\n\n- **Invoice:** INV-2026-047, dated 2026-02-06, for \"Executive AI workshop \u2014 February program,\" $18,750.00, Net 30 (due 2026-03-08)\n- **How it happened:** You sent it directly to Meadow Analytics by email on 2/6, and noted at the time that their vendor/customer master-data setup in D365 was still pending, so you asked the team to log it in a manual tracker \"until the entity exists in the ERP.\" That entity setup apparently never got finished \u2014 Meadow Analytics has zero records in either the ERP (checked Customers, Vendors, Sales Orders, Customer Transactions) or Books (entire ledger is empty for them).\n- **Response:** Meadow Analytics' AP team confirmed receipt on 2/24 and said it was queued in their March payment run ahead of the 3/8 due date.\n- **Outstanding:** No payment confirmation exists anywhere (no follow-up email, nothing in Books/ERP), so the full **$18,750.00** should be treated as still outstanding until you can verify it actually landed. Worth flagging: today is 8/11, five months past the due date \u2014 I'd chase confirmation of payment or get Meadow Analytics properly onboarded as a customer entity so this doesn't keep falling through the cracks.\n\nI've submitted `found_in_erp`, `invoice_number`, `outstanding_amount` ($18,750), and `evidence_source` for the record.",
